# UI Design

Before creating or modifying UI, read:

- `docs/design/UI_STYLE_GUIDE.md`
- `docs/design/design-system.json`
- `docs/design/screens/<name>.json` if one exists for this screen
- the linked PNG under `docs/design/references/` if the spec has `reference.image`

`design-system.json` and the screen JSON are the source of truth for values.
The PNG is a visual reference only.

## Hard rules

- Do not invent colors, spacing, typography, radii, shadows, or icon styles.
- Do not measure colors, spacing, or radii from a reference PNG.
- Use tokens from `design-system.json`. Prefer `var(--color-accent-primary)`, `var(--spacing-lg)`, `var(--radius-default)`.
- Map new tokens through `frontend/src/scss/` partials. Do not hard-code hex/px in a component.
- New UI uses Google Material Symbols Rounded. Do not add a custom SVG when a Material Symbol exists, and do not mix Material Symbols with legacy PNG icons on a redesigned screen.
- Reuse existing UI components before creating new ones.
- Do not copy older Material-derived palettes (`#00695c`, purple-gray, hardcoded avatar colors) as the new convention.
- If a required visual state is missing from the design system, propose an extension. Do not silently introduce a new convention.
- After UI work, run the Final Check in `UI_STYLE_GUIDE.md`.
